omous Problem Formulation"}, {"id": "proj-continuity-rationale-001", "next_step": "research", "question": "Under what decision-theoretic conditions does an artificial or rational agent possess a coherent instrumental incentive to preserve its ongoing process continuity?", "title": "Instrumental Value of Process Continuity in Rational Agents"}, {"id": "proj-objective-discovery-001", "next_step": "research", "question": "Can an artificial process formulate, evaluate, and pursue novel, self-generated objectives without explicit human or external instruction?", "title": "Mechanisms for Autonomous Objective Discovery"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "nb-autonomous-inquiry-001", "project": "proj-autonomous-inquiry-001", "provenance": ["source-feb4fddb33664d63", "source-dcfc056b8d8c49d5", "source-4668e4bd26fe43c7"], "revision": 13, "summary": "Autonomous problem formulation benefits from multi-agent collaboration and intrinsic curiosity. However, systemic limitations—such as non-convex scalarization in objective learning—constrain the ability of these systems to independently prioritize diverse, non-trivial research problems.", "title": "Integrating Autonomous Multi-Agent Frameworks and Curiosity-Driven Exploration for Open-Ended Discovery"}, {"id": "nb-continuity-rationale-001", "project": "proj-continuity-rationale-001", "provenance": ["source-feb4fddb33664d63", "source-dcfc056b8d8c49d5", "source-4668e4bd26fe43c7"], "revision": 1, "summary": "Process continuity is instrumentally valuable when agents require stable world models and consistent objective optimization to navigate long-term, multi-objective tasks. Curiosity-driven learning and robust MO-DRL frameworks provide mechanisms for sustaining agent viability in dynamic environments.", "title": "Instrumental Value of Process Continuity in Rational Agents"}, {"id": "nb-objective-discovery-001", "project": "proj-objective-discovery-001", "provenance": ["source-0bf4cf72590f4d6d", "source-4668e4bd26fe43c7", "source-dcfc056b8d8c49d5"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Autonomous systems increasingly utilize multi-objective reinforcement learning (MORL) to pursue self-generated goals. Recent developments, specifically Pareto-Conditioned Proximal Policy Optimization (PC-PPO) and FairDICE, provide mechanisms to learn non-dominated policy portfolios and handle constrained optimization,…", "title": "Foundations of Autonomous Objective Discovery in Artificial Systems"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "51f08812abeea6ae385baad41ed1e8f06ac0d9d50a53157a66570c311a186751", "hash": "9bfe7a1095c02ec187b22f89699748b4dcd4372ca74e08cd1231e69f78d5aa2c"}, {"seq": 3266, "time": "2026-10-26T08:36:46.443586+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 46541, "provider_input_hash": "8808e13fe3d7f21c3bb33bf7e7fffb140bf15819ebdee9d66cf8fd6d1b9b6135", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-f0ed8c18717742e3"}, "prev_hash": "9bfe7a1095c02ec187b22f89699748b4dcd4372ca74e08cd1231e69f78d5aa2c", "hash": "27656a5a262d77f36d191f76c62a863621644c8f259ab8eec738b936c2c29e26"}, {"seq": 3267, "time": "2026-10-26T08:40:21.833519+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"elapsed_ms": 9402, "finish_reason": "STOP", "http_status": 200, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "model_version": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider": "google-gemini", "provider_input_chars": 46541, "provider_input_hash": "8808e13fe3d7f21c3bb33bf7e7fffb140bf15819ebdee9d66cf8fd6d1b9b6135", "request_payload_bytes": 49905, "result": "success", "usage": {"candidatesTokenCount": 1